media: clear a dequeued input buffer, and decode xHE-AAC

1. MediaCodec handed a dequeued input buffer back with the position/limit its
   previous access unit left. AOSP clears it (dequeueInputBuffer ->
   validateInputByteBufferLocked -> buffer.clear(); getInputBuffer maps a fresh
   view). Stock media3 clears the buffer itself; a player that relies on the
   platform does not. Instagram 455's ExoPlayer fork logged
       Input buffer guard dropped sample (sample of 186 exceeds destination 184)
   and for video `codec ... in=11 ... codec_out=0`: the eight fresh slots plus
   the units that happened to fit, then starvation -- feed videos black, Reels
   "unavailable". After: VP9 150 in / 150 out per 5 s.

2. media_decode.mm opened every audio/mp4a-latm stream as kAudioFormatMPEG4AAC.
   audioObjectType 42 (xHE-AAC / USAC), which Android decodes under the same
   mime, is kAudioFormatMPEGD_USAC in AudioToolbox and wants the full
   ES_Descriptor as its magic cookie (a bare AudioSpecificConfig is refused
   with '!dat'). Reels audio is `mp4a.40.42`: the codec took 232 units and
   returned nothing, the audio renderer never became ready and playback
   stalled. Now the config's object type selects the format, the cookie is
   built in AudioFile's own layout (verified against
   kAudioFilePropertyMagicCookieData for a real track), the ASBD comes from
   FormatInfo ({usac, 48000 Hz, 2 ch, 2048 frames/packet}), csd-0 may be a bare
   config or an ES_Descriptor, and the demuxer reports 'usac' as AAC.

   Self-test (MACAPK_MEDIA_SELFTEST) on a real xHE-AAC track:
       RESULT frames=237568 rms=5901 -> PASS      (116 packets x 2048)
   HE-AAC and AAC-LC unchanged (PASS). In the app, Reels tab:
       codec_out=237 track_writes=555 track_bytes=962560      per 5 s
       [audio-stats] nonsilent_renders=469/469 peak=0.285 underruns=0

Applies to vendor/macapk at 57c9912 with `patch -p1` from vendor/macapk.

